    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d316">

                <pb facs="0297" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1949v09/pg287"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 Merchant, Livingston T.: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Stuart</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-02-14T19:00:00-05:00">February 14,
                            1949—7 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>211. For Merchant.<anchor n="75" xml:id="d316-f1"/> Dept wishes you to assume
                    special responsibility with respect to Taiwan. Wording in first sentence of
                    immediately <pb facs="0298" n="288" xml:id="pg288"/> following tel<anchor n="76"
                        xml:id="d316-f2"/> is occasioned by accounting regulations. Dept desires you
                    retain title of Counselor of Emb and indicate that you are merely going to
                    Taiwan to oversee expanded US representation on that island which milit events
                    on mainland have occasioned and in particular with respect to ECA. Implication
                    that you have been transferred Taipei should be avoided. Accordingly you should
                    feel free to visit Nanking and Shanghai but should not find yourself immobilized
                    on mainland should Nanking or Shanghai pass into hands of Commies.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
